proton-autogen (3.3.6) noble; urgency=medium

  * Thanks to all users and contributors for their continued support, feedback and bug reports.
  * Support for additional Linux distributions.
  * Improved Lutris profile management.
  * Improved save management.
  * New application and UI icons.
  * More responsive game list and interface.
  * Improved KIO and Nemo integration.
  * More stable Helper and diagnostic tools.
  * Improved profile stability.
  * Updated installation documentation.
  * Fixed executable path handling with Nemo 6.6.3.
  * Fixed paths containing spaces or special characters when launching games from Nemo.
  * Fixed several UI layout and display issues
  * Add game save management (Memory) to preserve and restore application data.
  * Add new proton-autogen --import command (Beta) to import and recover games from Lutris and other supported sources.
  * Add system sleep inhibition while games are running
  * Added settings menu with all application options.
  * Advanced ProtonDB evolution. Integrated menu.
  * Add ProtonDB integration with game compatibility ratings, confidence levels and report counts.
  * Add support for displaying ProtonDB compatibility information directly in the game list and grid.
  * Add support for editing the Steam App ID from the application editor.
  * Improve application responsiveness and adaptive layout behavior.
  * Add a dedicated GRID menu with zoom controls for adjusting game icon sizes.
  * Improve the GRID layout with adaptive column handling and responsive game cards.
  * Add visual feedback for game card interactions and improve the overall GRID user experience.
  * Automatically save and restore the application window size between sessions.
  * Add a status bar message history panel, allowing users to review all status messages since startup with timestamps and a clear action.
  * Add a dedicated status message widget with support for expandable details, allowing truncated messages to be viewed and copied in full.
  * Improve status bar readability by limiting long multi-line messages to 6 lines and indicating when additional lines are available in the history.
  * Fix broken raw ANSI escape sequences being displayed in the status bar when applications emit colored console output.
  * Fix excessive CPU usage during application launches caused by the status bar rebuilding its entire message history on every spinner animation frame.
  * Fix a significant CPU usage issue during application execution where every line of process output (stdout/stderr) triggered an immediate status bar update.
  * Reduce CPU overhead of status message processing by consolidating multiple regular expressions into single combined patterns, without changing observable behavior.
  * Improve application terminology throughout the interface, replacing game-specific wording with application-specific terminology to better reflect support for generic Windows programs.
  * Localize the application search entry placeholder instead of using hardcoded text.
  * Update all 16 supported locale files.
  * Improve graphical user experience with clearer status reporting and easier access to detailed application launch information.
  * Internal UX improvements with the introduction of dedicated status bar and status history handling.
  * General UX improvements, configuration handling improvements and code cleanup.

 -- N3oray <n3oray77@gmail.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 12:28:00 +0200
